1
00:00:02,530 --> 00:00:03,980
Terrible...

2
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:08,410
I'm not referring to your behavior.

3
00:00:08,850 --> 00:00:12,150
I was simply overwhelmed 
with rage at the one

4
00:00:12,630 --> 00:00:14,990
who put you through so much hardship.

5
00:00:16,080 --> 00:00:16,870
Me?

6
00:00:18,240 --> 00:00:19,580
The Witch of Envy...

7
00:00:21,870 --> 00:00:23,630
I'm sure you were aware

8
00:00:23,630 --> 00:00:27,240
that the power you have is that of a witch.

9
00:00:27,240 --> 00:00:28,840
You've known for a long time.

10
00:00:29,690 --> 00:00:33,090
Well, I've sure had plenty of 
people telling me about a witch.

11
00:00:33,860 --> 00:00:37,930
I have no idea why she's 
so fixated on me, though.

12
00:00:38,240 --> 00:00:42,620
No one is capable of understanding 
how her mind works.

13
00:00:43,190 --> 00:00:46,080
Even if I could, I wouldn't want to.

14
00:00:47,130 --> 00:00:47,940
Hey...

15
00:00:49,400 --> 00:00:53,260
Do you think there's a limit to how many 
times Return by Death can be used?

16
00:00:53,260 --> 00:00:56,970
Ah, yes. Truly the obvious question to ask.

17
00:00:57,460 --> 00:01:00,550
I will say in advance that 
this is only conjecture,

18
00:01:01,940 --> 00:01:03,060
but I would say...

19
00:01:04,120 --> 00:01:04,960
there isn't.

20
00:01:12,530 --> 00:01:16,250
Vexing as it may seem, the power 
that lets you Return by Death

21
00:01:16,250 --> 00:01:17,910
is the witch's intense delusion.

22
00:01:17,910 --> 00:01:21,580
So long as that delusion persists, 
there will be no end to your deaths.

23
00:01:21,580 --> 00:01:23,960
Do you have any idea why 
she gave me this power?

24
00:01:24,780 --> 00:01:27,190
So that you won't die.

25
00:01:27,600 --> 00:01:31,650
It makes you redo destiny and doesn't 
allow you to make mistakes.

26
00:01:32,190 --> 00:01:33,900
That can't be right.

27
00:01:34,560 --> 00:01:36,360
I mean, I...

28
00:01:37,740 --> 00:01:39,370
couldn't get Rem back.

29
00:01:40,860 --> 00:01:42,910
If she's making me redo destiny,

30
00:01:42,910 --> 00:01:44,950
why'd I end up in a place 
that made it irreversible?

31
00:01:44,950 --> 00:01:49,290
Because that girl was not taken into 
account as part of that destiny.

32
00:01:49,680 --> 00:01:55,080
Her hope is that you will never be trapped 
by the dead end that is true death.

33
00:01:55,080 --> 00:01:57,940
Anyone who isn't you is 
not part of the plan.

34
00:01:58,450 --> 00:02:01,670
The decision to go to such lengths 
to save someone else with your power

35
00:02:01,670 --> 00:02:03,510
is yours and yours alone.

36
00:02:04,520 --> 00:02:08,560
You will overcome destiny through 
countless challenges henceforth,

37
00:02:09,280 --> 00:02:15,320
but if you do change destiny at 
the expense of many sacrifices...

38
00:02:16,470 --> 00:02:21,150
I won't have any chances to get 
back those who were sacrificed.

39
00:02:22,960 --> 00:02:24,720
That's how it is.

40
00:02:34,010 --> 00:02:35,160
Fine.

41
00:02:35,600 --> 00:02:39,690
If you insist on reserving 
that favor for me alone,

42
00:02:39,690 --> 00:02:41,220
then I know what I have to do.

43
00:02:41,920 --> 00:02:44,720
I'll use this Return by 
Death blessing you gave me

44
00:02:45,720 --> 00:02:47,810
until there's nothing left to use!

45
00:02:48,080 --> 00:02:50,690
Yeah, that's it. I've made up my mind.

46
00:02:51,260 --> 00:02:55,570
No one's better than me at 
betraying people's expectations!

47
00:02:56,490 --> 00:02:59,400
You bounced back with surprising ease.

48
00:02:59,850 --> 00:03:01,850
It wasn't easy at all.

49
00:03:01,850 --> 00:03:03,360
If I did what I've always done,

50
00:03:03,360 --> 00:03:06,590
I might've tried to tape my broken 
heart back together in desperation.

51
00:03:07,280 --> 00:03:08,780
But now...

52
00:03:15,090 --> 00:03:17,770
What is it? Aren't you going to finish?

53
00:03:18,190 --> 00:03:19,610
Well? Aren't you?

54
00:03:19,610 --> 00:03:22,280
You know damn well what I was gonna say!

55
00:03:22,640 --> 00:03:25,930
Anyway, your input has 
been very informative.

56
00:03:25,930 --> 00:03:28,080
It helped me make up my mind, too.

57
00:03:28,080 --> 00:03:29,430
So thanks for that.

58
00:03:30,430 --> 00:03:31,960
Just for that?

59
00:03:31,960 --> 00:03:36,940
That's all you want to thank me for 
after sharing your secret with me?

60
00:03:37,680 --> 00:03:41,190
Shut up! Why are you so determined 
to make me thank you?!

61
00:03:41,190 --> 00:03:44,560
You should be trying to make me ask 
you questions, like last time!

62
00:03:46,400 --> 00:03:48,360
You're the only one I can count on.

63
00:03:48,360 --> 00:03:50,420
I'll pay whatever price you want.

64
00:03:52,680 --> 00:03:56,170
You just might have a knack 
for seducing witches.

65
00:03:56,680 --> 00:03:58,750
Well? What would you like to ask me?

66
00:03:59,280 --> 00:04:01,410
There's too much I don't know.

67
00:04:01,410 --> 00:04:04,510
First and foremost, right now
 is that last moment...

68
00:04:05,400 --> 00:04:07,470
when I died by being eaten.

69
00:04:08,420 --> 00:04:10,480
Those rabbits could've fit in my hand.

70
00:04:10,480 --> 00:04:13,080
Ah, you mean the Great Rabbit.

71
00:04:13,080 --> 00:04:14,190
"Great" Rabbit?

72
00:04:14,760 --> 00:04:17,770
Great not in size, but in number.

73
00:04:18,160 --> 00:04:20,680
It's one of the Three Great Mabeasts.

74
00:04:20,680 --> 00:04:22,280
Three Great Mabeasts?

75
00:04:22,280 --> 00:04:25,280
The White Whale, the Black 
Serpent, and the Great Rabbit.

76
00:04:26,070 --> 00:04:30,370
They were created 400 years ago 
by Daphne, the Witch of Gluttony.

77
00:04:30,780 --> 00:04:34,870
Her three legacies of misfortune, which still
 bring disaster upon the world today.

78
00:04:34,870 --> 00:04:36,560
You've gotta be kidding me!

79
00:04:36,560 --> 00:04:39,480
I just managed to fish up the 
White Whale not long ago!

80
00:04:39,480 --> 00:04:41,480
There's more to this unpleasant story.

81
00:04:42,310 --> 00:04:44,540
In terms of pure fighting strength,

82
00:04:44,540 --> 00:04:46,740
the White Whale is far stronger.

83
00:04:46,740 --> 00:04:51,300
But the Great Rabbit is infinitely 
more difficult to destroy.

84
00:04:51,750 --> 00:04:55,400
To the Great Rabbit, all other 
living things are food.

85
00:04:55,960 --> 00:04:59,710
It desires nothing other 
than to satisfy its hunger.

86
00:04:59,710 --> 00:05:02,800
All it leaves behind is a deserted field.

87
00:05:02,800 --> 00:05:04,280
Deserted... field?

88
00:05:04,760 --> 00:05:06,950
You don't mean all of that was...

89
00:05:08,200 --> 00:05:11,510
What makes the Great Rabbit so 
difficult is its viability.

90
00:05:11,930 --> 00:05:15,670
A single one is capable of 
multiplying infinitely.

91
00:05:15,670 --> 00:05:18,330
Infinitely? What is it, an amoeba?

92
00:05:18,780 --> 00:05:23,870
To destroy it, you'd have to kill 
every last one at the same time,

93
00:05:24,300 --> 00:05:28,830
and that would be like trying to evaporate 
every raindrop that falls from the sky.

94
00:05:28,830 --> 00:05:31,030
What choice do we have but to run, then?!

95
00:05:31,030 --> 00:05:33,560
No... That won't work. The barrier's there.

96
00:05:34,160 --> 00:05:37,730
So long as the barrier's there, 
Emilia and the others can't leave.

97
00:05:37,960 --> 00:05:39,770
The Great Rabbit in the Sanctuary,

98
00:05:40,210 --> 00:05:41,650
the attack on the mansion...

99
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:45,570
I have to break the barrier and free 
them before any of that happens.

100
00:05:45,570 --> 00:05:49,620
Then I'll gather everyone at the mansion 
to defeat Elsa and the mabeasts.

101
00:05:49,850 --> 00:05:51,030
I have...

102
00:05:51,260 --> 00:05:53,370
Though, since you came back 
sooner than expected,

103
00:05:53,650 --> 00:05:57,080
this didn't play out exactly 
as my directions specified.

104
00:05:57,820 --> 00:05:59,910
...four days, then?

105
00:06:02,240 --> 00:06:05,040
Echidna? Do you know of a way?

106
00:06:06,180 --> 00:06:10,000
It carries such great risk that 
I hesitate to suggest it...

107
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:13,460
But what if I told you that 
I could give you an opportunity

108
00:06:13,460 --> 00:06:15,620
to talk to Daphne, the Witch of Gluttony?

109
00:06:15,620 --> 00:06:16,390
Huh?

110
00:06:16,800 --> 00:06:19,570
I thought all the other witches were dead.

111
00:06:19,570 --> 00:06:23,070
Then how do you explain the one 
speaking to you right now?

112
00:06:23,070 --> 00:06:27,630
The souls of the dead witches reside 
with me in this castle of dreams.

113
00:06:27,630 --> 00:06:28,480
In other words...

114
00:06:28,480 --> 00:06:30,360
You can call her here?

115
00:06:30,860 --> 00:06:33,580
If I let her temporarily 
inhabit my presence.

116
00:06:34,080 --> 00:06:37,370
During that time, they and 
I literally trade places.

117
00:06:38,480 --> 00:06:41,380
But I really don't recommend it.

118
00:06:41,920 --> 00:06:44,680
There is no death in this dimension,

119
00:06:44,680 --> 00:06:48,040
but if your mind sustains an 
injury that causes it to break,

120
00:06:48,040 --> 00:06:51,120
it will remain shattered even 
after you return to your body.

121
00:06:51,120 --> 00:06:54,160
So I'd become an invalid?

122
00:06:54,160 --> 00:06:56,890
That's a way bigger risk 
than I'd be taking outside.

123
00:06:56,890 --> 00:06:58,260
Do you decline, then?

124
00:07:01,420 --> 00:07:03,840
She's the one who created 
the Great Rabbit, right?

125
00:07:03,840 --> 00:07:07,320
So she'd be the best one to ask 
for ideas on how to defeat it.

126
00:07:09,970 --> 00:07:11,280
Do it.

127
00:07:12,340 --> 00:07:14,530
Your resolve is firm, then?

128
00:07:14,920 --> 00:07:17,350
But just let me say one thing first.

129
00:07:17,770 --> 00:07:21,290
No matter what you do, 
don't release Daphne's restraints.

130
00:07:21,290 --> 00:07:22,610
Restraints?

131
00:07:22,610 --> 00:07:25,380
You are also forbidden to touch her.

132
00:07:25,640 --> 00:07:28,520
You should avoid eye contact, too, if possible.

133
00:07:28,520 --> 00:07:32,300
Avoiding all that would make me 
come across as a total jerk!

134
00:07:33,090 --> 00:07:34,660
I wish you the best.

135
00:07:42,820 --> 00:07:45,240
Ah! We meet at last!

136
00:07:45,240 --> 00:07:45,730
Huh?

137
00:07:46,290 --> 00:07:48,750
What do you mean, "huh"?!

138
00:07:48,750 --> 00:07:51,680
That's very rude, you know!

139
00:07:51,680 --> 00:07:52,320
Hmph!

140
00:07:53,220 --> 00:07:57,280
You're a... I mean, you're 
also a witch, right?

141
00:07:57,280 --> 00:07:59,870
Chidna told you, didn't she?

142
00:07:59,870 --> 00:08:01,160
And you're...

143
00:08:01,660 --> 00:08:04,670
Let's see... Baru! Baru, right?

144
00:08:05,150 --> 00:08:06,040
Baru?

145
00:08:06,040 --> 00:08:08,650
Are you a bad guy, Baru?

146
00:08:08,650 --> 00:08:11,480
I've wondered about that this whole time!

147
00:08:11,480 --> 00:08:12,510
A bad guy?

148
00:08:13,850 --> 00:08:15,460
You want me to hold it?

149
00:08:15,920 --> 00:08:18,500
Wait, no! There's something I want to ask—

150
00:08:19,170 --> 00:08:21,130
Okay, okay! Fine!

151
00:08:22,220 --> 00:08:25,720
Sin can only be repaid with pain.

152
00:08:27,130 --> 00:08:27,480
Huh?

153
00:08:27,850 --> 00:08:32,280
Oh! If you don't feel pain, 
you must not be a bad guy!

154
00:08:32,280 --> 00:08:33,950
That's great!

155
00:08:39,400 --> 00:08:41,110
My arm!

156
00:08:40,220 --> 00:08:41,680
But it doesn't hurt, does it?

157
00:08:41,680 --> 00:08:44,540
If you make too much noise, 
Chidna's gonna hate you.

158
00:08:44,540 --> 00:08:46,470
Damn you!

159
00:08:46,470 --> 00:08:48,240
Give it back!

160
00:08:48,240 --> 00:08:51,240
Sin will become a wedge 
that allows no escape.

161
00:08:55,050 --> 00:08:59,740
So you see yourself as a sinner, 
even though you're not a bad guy?

162
00:08:59,740 --> 00:09:01,430
You have such a good heart, Baru!

163
00:09:01,780 --> 00:09:03,560
You poor thing.

164
00:09:04,080 --> 00:09:06,670
Well, that's all Typhon came here for.

165
00:09:07,120 --> 00:09:08,320
That leaves...

166
00:09:10,900 --> 00:09:14,030
First! To strike all that 
defies reason in the world!

167
00:09:14,700 --> 00:09:18,780
Second! Who cares about committing 
every heinous evildoing?!

168
00:09:19,060 --> 00:09:22,160
Third! Whether it's ugly or beautiful,

169
00:09:22,160 --> 00:09:24,640
if you're here in this fleeting world,

170
00:09:24,640 --> 00:09:28,670
don't expect to make it back unscathed!

171
00:09:30,600 --> 00:09:33,300
My fist will restore the world!

172
00:09:33,300 --> 00:09:35,670
My anger will cleanse the world!

173
00:09:35,950 --> 00:09:39,240
My rage, the fury of my fists,

174
00:09:39,240 --> 00:09:41,540
shall be my answer!

175
00:09:47,320 --> 00:09:49,070
Why are you crying?

176
00:09:49,070 --> 00:09:51,480
I'm not crying! I'm just angry!

177
00:09:51,890 --> 00:09:54,230
That's right! I'm angry!

178
00:09:54,230 --> 00:09:56,840
It's Typhon's fault for 
hurting you like that!

179
00:09:56,840 --> 00:09:58,190
Stupid Typhon!

180
00:09:58,590 --> 00:10:00,910
I hate this world for making her do that!

181
00:10:00,910 --> 00:10:02,640
I hate all of it!

182
00:10:01,830 --> 00:10:04,560
Uh... Thanks for saving me...

183
00:10:04,560 --> 00:10:05,870
Um, and you are...?

184
00:10:07,550 --> 00:10:09,730
I'm the Witch of Wrath, Minerva!

185
00:10:09,730 --> 00:10:11,320
My name isn't worth giving!

186
00:10:11,320 --> 00:10:12,920
But you just did!

187
00:10:14,380 --> 00:10:15,490
Listen up!

188
00:10:15,490 --> 00:10:18,270
If you've learned your lesson, 
don't do anything careless!

189
00:10:18,270 --> 00:10:20,360
Next time, I'll just heal everyone!

190
00:10:20,360 --> 00:10:22,620
Don't make it sound like a threat!

191
00:10:24,880 --> 00:10:26,770
What's going on here?

192
00:10:26,770 --> 00:10:30,990
Typhon? Minerva? This 
isn't what we agreed—

193
00:10:34,600 --> 00:10:36,120
Oh, come on...

194
00:10:40,920 --> 00:10:45,120
What would you like to ask of Daphne,

195
00:10:45,840 --> 00:10:47,430
Subarun?

196
00:10:51,080 --> 00:10:54,560
I'm here because Chid-Chid asked me to come,

197
00:10:54,560 --> 00:10:57,950
but I don't want to be awake 
any longer than I have to be,

198
00:10:57,950 --> 00:11:00,760
so please don't drag this 
out with dull conversation.

199
00:11:02,810 --> 00:11:06,470
Oh... This might be toxic to me...

200
00:11:08,420 --> 00:11:10,060
Wh-What the heck?

201
00:11:10,520 --> 00:11:12,940
My body is throbbing.

202
00:11:13,350 --> 00:11:18,650
You give off a scent that 
I really, really love...

203
00:11:19,280 --> 00:11:22,420
It's making me want to eat you.

204
00:11:24,400 --> 00:11:26,740
Then let's just make this quick.

205
00:11:27,180 --> 00:11:30,060
I want to talk about the Three 
Great Mabeasts that you made.

206
00:11:31,020 --> 00:11:32,960
The Three Great Mabeasts?

207
00:11:33,390 --> 00:11:37,560
The White Whale, the Great Rabbit, 
and the Black Serpent or whatever!

208
00:11:37,560 --> 00:11:39,420
You made them, didn't you?

209
00:11:40,090 --> 00:11:44,390
Oh, the whale, the bunny, and the snake?

210
00:11:44,390 --> 00:11:47,300
Why in the world did you make those things?

211
00:11:47,300 --> 00:11:49,220
Huh? What was that?

212
00:11:49,410 --> 00:11:53,560
Why did you set those things 
loose on the world?!

213
00:11:53,560 --> 00:11:55,440
Do you realize what they've...

214
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:58,600
Why did you do it?!

215
00:11:58,600 --> 00:12:01,990
Why did you make monsters like those?!

216
00:12:03,050 --> 00:12:06,530
The White Whale is very big, isn't it?

217
00:12:06,530 --> 00:12:10,810
It would sate so many appetites if 
people ate it, don't you think?

218
00:12:10,810 --> 00:12:11,200
Huh?

219
00:12:11,550 --> 00:12:15,500
And the Great Rabbit can 
multiply itself indefinitely.

220
00:12:16,020 --> 00:12:17,630
With them around,

221
00:12:17,840 --> 00:12:21,280
no one would ever have to go hungry.

222
00:12:21,280 --> 00:12:24,770
I'm saying that your Great Rabbit 
is the one eating everybody!

223
00:12:24,770 --> 00:12:27,100
These mabeasts are taking more people 
away than they're feeding—

224
00:12:27,100 --> 00:12:29,310
Don't you think it's a bit selfish

225
00:12:29,590 --> 00:12:32,890
to try to eat another without considering

226
00:12:32,890 --> 00:12:35,560
the possibility of being eaten yourself?

227
00:12:35,560 --> 00:12:37,540
The same goes for you, Subarun.

228
00:12:37,540 --> 00:12:41,260
Don't you think everyone 
takes gluttony too lightly?

229
00:12:41,680 --> 00:12:42,990
The appetite is

230
00:12:43,420 --> 00:12:47,200
the most important of all the 
desires that keep people alive.

231
00:12:47,560 --> 00:12:49,560
Even if the heart feels sated,

232
00:12:49,560 --> 00:12:54,780
people die if they don't eat.

233
00:12:55,210 --> 00:12:58,920
What you're saying is partly right, but—

234
00:12:58,920 --> 00:13:04,130
You'll understand, too, if you 
are starved to your limit.

235
00:13:04,130 --> 00:13:07,430
You'll see what sort of world 
my bunny and I live in.

236
00:13:07,720 --> 00:13:11,250
If I told you I wanted to get 
rid of your Great Rabbit,

237
00:13:11,250 --> 00:13:12,890
would you give me any tips?

238
00:13:13,400 --> 00:13:18,430
The Great Rabbit relies 
on mana to find its prey.

239
00:13:19,480 --> 00:13:20,650
You really don't mind?

240
00:13:21,160 --> 00:13:23,600
If we must eat to stay alive,

241
00:13:23,600 --> 00:13:28,740
it wouldn't make sense to deny 
that we must kill to survive.

242
00:13:29,670 --> 00:13:33,890
It's naturally drawn to places 
that have a lot of mana,

243
00:13:33,890 --> 00:13:36,920
so you could use a powerful 
magic user as a lure,

244
00:13:36,920 --> 00:13:40,000
then wipe them all out at 
once when they gather there.

245
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:42,360
I heard it can multiply indefinitely.

246
00:13:42,360 --> 00:13:44,380
Won't there be some that 
separate from the group?

247
00:13:45,010 --> 00:13:49,070
There may be many of them, but 
they all share one consciousness.

248
00:13:49,070 --> 00:13:53,670
They don't have the wisdom to 
avoid being killed or anything.

249
00:13:56,010 --> 00:13:58,770
Are you finished with me now?

250
00:13:59,320 --> 00:14:00,320
Yeah.

251
00:14:00,320 --> 00:14:03,530
I still don't get why you created 
them, but I've learned a lot.

252
00:14:03,960 --> 00:14:05,030
Thanks.

253
00:14:05,840 --> 00:14:06,740
Also...

254
00:14:07,410 --> 00:14:09,880
I will destroy the Great Rabbit.

255
00:14:09,880 --> 00:14:12,110
I already killed the White Whale, after all.

256
00:14:12,110 --> 00:14:13,490
You'd better not come crying to me,

257
00:14:13,930 --> 00:14:15,320
"Mother."

258
00:14:16,360 --> 00:14:19,560
Those things have been running 
rampant for 400 years.

259
00:14:19,560 --> 00:14:21,320
That's long enough.

260
00:14:21,320 --> 00:14:23,270
I'm gonna wipe them out without a trace.

261
00:14:24,500 --> 00:14:26,700
If you think a mere human...

262
00:14:31,470 --> 00:14:35,810
is capable of that, then 
go ahead and try it.

263
00:14:47,090 --> 00:14:51,630
Seeing your face is such a relief, it's 
like being back home with my family.

264
00:14:51,630 --> 00:14:54,400
That's a somewhat confusing 
way to describe it.

265
00:14:54,400 --> 00:14:56,360
I was a bit disconcerted, too,

266
00:14:56,360 --> 00:15:00,290
when Typhon jumped in the moment
I tried to give my body to Daphne.

267
00:15:00,830 --> 00:15:02,160
Oh, her?

268
00:15:02,160 --> 00:15:04,430
Yes, the Witch of Pride.

269
00:15:04,430 --> 00:15:06,130
She's very much a child, as you saw.

270
00:15:06,520 --> 00:15:09,490
She was so eager to meet you 
that she jumped right out.

271
00:15:10,670 --> 00:15:14,850
And the one who saved you was 
the Witch of Wrath, Minerva.

272
00:15:15,610 --> 00:15:20,310
So? Did Daphne give you 
any useful information?

273
00:15:21,160 --> 00:15:22,740
Yeah, sort of.

274
00:15:22,740 --> 00:15:27,360
First of all, I learned that you're 
the most normal of the witches.

275
00:15:27,940 --> 00:15:30,940
Oh, please. Just stop already.

276
00:15:30,940 --> 00:15:34,750
You're just trying to butter 
me up with pleasing words.

277
00:15:34,750 --> 00:15:37,370
Don't underestimate me like that.

278
00:15:38,580 --> 00:15:41,040
You're like an open book, you know that?

279
00:15:41,480 --> 00:15:44,770
But I'll pass on your bodily 
fluids and cookies.

280
00:15:44,770 --> 00:15:46,800
I didn't put any hair in it.

281
00:15:46,800 --> 00:15:50,920
I can't even trust a single 
thing you say anymore.

282
00:15:52,960 --> 00:15:53,880
What was...

283
00:15:53,880 --> 00:15:57,380
Looks like it's nearly 
time for you to wake up.

284
00:15:57,380 --> 00:15:59,770
Perhaps something happened outside 
to speed your awakening?

285
00:16:03,280 --> 00:16:05,740
You mean... Emilia?

286
00:16:05,740 --> 00:16:10,990
No, wait... Weren't you passing yourself 
off as the examiner for the trial?

287
00:16:11,190 --> 00:16:12,910
So why are you here?

288
00:16:12,910 --> 00:16:15,260
Emilia should be undergoing 
the trial right now!

289
00:16:15,260 --> 00:16:17,990
Because the result is already in sight.

290
00:16:18,680 --> 00:16:20,700
The result is in sight?

291
00:16:21,070 --> 00:16:24,790
I'm saying I have no interest 
in the result of her challenge.

292
00:16:25,170 --> 00:16:26,540
Even in three days of trial and error,

293
00:16:26,540 --> 00:16:29,940
I can't hold out any hope that 
she'll break out of her shell.

294
00:16:31,040 --> 00:16:31,920
Or perhaps...

295
00:16:32,360 --> 00:16:34,130
<i>you</i> could do it?

296
00:16:34,600 --> 00:16:37,590
Since you've made up your mind 
to keep repeating everything,

297
00:16:37,590 --> 00:16:40,560
could you give wings to 
the cowardly princess?

298
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:43,640
I hate that it feels like 
I'm letting you provoke me,

299
00:16:43,640 --> 00:16:46,740
but I won't let you make Emilia cry any more.

300
00:16:46,740 --> 00:16:50,380
Oh, no. I'm not the one making her cry.

301
00:16:50,380 --> 00:16:53,580
I'll go through your sadistic trial.

302
00:16:53,580 --> 00:16:55,160
That was my plan to begin with.

303
00:16:55,460 --> 00:16:59,570
I hardly think it's necessary 
to call it sadistic.

304
00:16:59,570 --> 00:17:02,870
Echidna, how can I come here again?

305
00:17:04,180 --> 00:17:06,060
I know I'm being selfish,

306
00:17:06,060 --> 00:17:09,420
but I want to be able to 
seek your wisdom again.

307
00:17:09,850 --> 00:17:12,460
You know a lot, and...

308
00:17:12,860 --> 00:17:15,680
And I know about your Return by Death power.

309
00:17:16,370 --> 00:17:17,870
Yeah, exactly.

310
00:17:18,550 --> 00:17:21,520
It does feel nice to be depended on,

311
00:17:21,520 --> 00:17:24,940
but I think that would be rather difficult.

312
00:17:25,400 --> 00:17:28,670
The conditions to attend the witch's 
tea party grow stricter each time,

313
00:17:29,300 --> 00:17:32,310
and you have already been invited twice.

314
00:17:32,680 --> 00:17:36,100
If you cry out "I want to know" 
from the bottom of your heart,

315
00:17:36,100 --> 00:17:37,800
your voice will reach me.

316
00:17:37,800 --> 00:17:41,200
It'll need to be even louder the 
third time than the second.

317
00:17:41,570 --> 00:17:42,960
Think you can do that?

318
00:17:44,590 --> 00:17:48,760
Of course, if you do undergo 
the trial, as you hope to,

319
00:17:48,760 --> 00:17:50,670
that won't be the only way.

320
00:17:51,760 --> 00:17:55,770
That's right! I can see you 
within the trial, too!

321
00:17:55,770 --> 00:17:58,380
I doubt it'll be over tea, though.

322
00:17:58,730 --> 00:18:00,750
Well, if you really insist...

323
00:18:00,750 --> 00:18:02,470
No, that's okay!

324
00:18:03,610 --> 00:18:07,190
Oh, crap... I'm really 
starting to feel faint.

325
00:18:07,540 --> 00:18:09,760
Echidna, one more thing before I go...

326
00:18:11,040 --> 00:18:14,270
The payment to make sure I don't 
forget what happened here!

327
00:18:14,270 --> 00:18:15,650
You need that, right?

328
00:18:15,650 --> 00:18:17,620
Oh... Oh, the payment!

329
00:18:18,040 --> 00:18:20,900
Of course, I wouldn't 
want you to forget this.

330
00:18:21,840 --> 00:18:23,080
In that case...

331
00:18:24,380 --> 00:18:25,940
I think I'll take this.

332
00:18:27,050 --> 00:18:30,950
Really? But it's just a handkerchief.

333
00:18:30,950 --> 00:18:32,460
Besides, it's...

334
00:18:32,460 --> 00:18:35,930
No need to worry. This world 
exists within the mind.

335
00:18:35,930 --> 00:18:38,760
It won't be gone once you're back outside.

336
00:18:40,340 --> 00:18:42,390
How does it work as payment, then?

337
00:18:42,880 --> 00:18:47,180
The one who gave you this did so 
out of heartfelt concern for you.

338
00:18:47,540 --> 00:18:49,740
It wouldn't do to ridicule that sentiment.

339
00:18:50,320 --> 00:18:53,180
This payment is recognition 
of that person's existence,

340
00:18:53,650 --> 00:18:55,570
and perhaps a bit of meddling, as well.

341
00:19:02,850 --> 00:19:03,770
Payment received.

342
00:19:07,560 --> 00:19:09,230
Okay, thanks again.

343
00:19:09,680 --> 00:19:11,790
See you in the trial, I guess.

344
00:19:12,880 --> 00:19:14,220
Natsuki Subaru...

345
00:19:14,620 --> 00:19:18,300
If you do attend the witch's 
tea party a third time...

346
00:19:19,510 --> 00:19:24,620
This time, there's something 
I would like to tell <i>you</i>.

347
00:19:31,320 --> 00:19:33,480
Do I have to go through this every time?

348
00:19:35,400 --> 00:19:36,820
I remember.

349
00:19:37,240 --> 00:19:40,660
I guess Echidna kept her promise, then.

350
00:19:41,370 --> 00:19:44,270
I swear, that so-called 
"witch" is just a big fraud.

351
00:19:44,760 --> 00:19:47,260
I'm gonna be counting on you for now.

352
00:19:51,830 --> 00:19:54,300
Emilia wasn't the one waking me up?

353
00:19:55,440 --> 00:19:58,960
Wait... she didn't run outside 
in a panic, did she?!

354
00:20:03,630 --> 00:20:04,300
Huh?

355
00:20:09,570 --> 00:20:10,480
A shadow?

356
00:20:12,870 --> 00:20:13,560
Emilia!

357
00:20:14,410 --> 00:20:15,840
Emilia, where are you?!

358
00:20:15,840 --> 00:20:17,360
Please, answer me!

359
00:20:17,360 --> 00:20:20,780
Ram! Ryuzu-san! Even you, Otto!

360
00:20:20,780 --> 00:20:23,300
You're there, right? Get out here!

361
00:20:43,430 --> 00:20:44,800
You're...

362
00:20:46,840 --> 00:20:47,680
I love you.

363
00:20:48,610 --> 00:20:50,600
I love you. I love you.

364
00:20:51,130 --> 00:20:52,350
I love you.

365
00:20:52,950 --> 00:20:53,770
I love you.

366
00:20:54,870 --> 00:20:55,900
I love you.

367
00:20:57,060 --> 00:20:58,150
I love you.

368
00:20:58,820 --> 00:21:00,150
I love you.

369
00:21:00,150 --> 00:21:02,570
I love you... I love you... I love you...

370
00:21:02,570 --> 00:21:07,570
Love Love Love Love Love Love You

371
00:21:02,570 --> 00:21:07,570
Love Love Love Love Love Love You

372
00:21:02,570 --> 00:21:07,570
Love Love Love Love Love Love You

373
00:21:02,570 --> 00:21:07,570
Love Love Love Love Love Love You

374
00:21:02,570 --> 00:21:07,570
Love Love Love Love Love Love You

375
00:21:05,700 --> 00:21:07,170
I love you.

376
00:21:13,180 --> 00:21:16,040
Quit screwin' around!

377
00:21:21,460 --> 00:21:22,530
We're gonna jump!

378
00:21:35,970 --> 00:21:36,980
You!

379
00:21:37,340 --> 00:21:40,360
What? You got a problem?

380
00:21:41,760 --> 00:21:44,280
No, I don't have a problem.

381
00:21:44,770 --> 00:21:47,830
I just wasn't expecting you to save me.

382
00:21:48,220 --> 00:21:50,540
Can't you see what's goin' on?

383
00:21:50,940 --> 00:21:54,690
What's important right now is findin' 
a way to bite off that thing's head!

384
00:21:54,690 --> 00:21:55,860
Nothin' else!

385
00:21:57,160 --> 00:22:00,710
What the hell... Why now, of all times?

386
00:22:01,090 --> 00:22:04,090
Why are you here,

387
00:22:04,810 --> 00:22:06,550
Witch of Envy?!

388
00:22:07,030 --> 00:22:10,470
Think... Think, think, think!

389
00:22:10,470 --> 00:22:13,360
I have to do something... 
I have to beat her somehow...

390
00:22:13,360 --> 00:22:16,230
The bitch isn't tryin' to follow us?

391
00:22:17,740 --> 00:22:20,770
What? She gonna leave the barrier?

392
00:22:23,870 --> 00:22:25,280
The mansion...

393
00:22:25,790 --> 00:22:27,020
The mansion!

394
00:22:27,020 --> 00:22:30,320
That witch is heading for Roswaal's mansion!

395
00:22:30,320 --> 00:22:31,480
The hell'd you say?!

396
00:22:32,080 --> 00:22:36,100
I'm not letting you get 
away with anything else!

397
00:24:07,820 --> 00:24:11,590
Goodness. What terrible luck.

398
00:24:12,230 --> 00:24:16,140
And without even knowing the 
outcome of the trial...

399
00:24:17,340 --> 00:24:19,820
If you wish to walk through Hell,

400
00:24:20,290 --> 00:24:22,600
I will gladly accompany you.

401
00:24:25,330 --> 00:24:27,730
If you wish to live in Hell,

402
00:24:28,160 --> 00:24:31,020
then Hell is what I shall strive for.

403
00:24:32,040 --> 00:24:35,040
Try not to make any mistakes next time,

404
00:24:35,500 --> 00:24:37,440
Natsuki Subaru.

405
00:24:37,440 --> 00:24:47,440


